    ".DISK",
    "Linux Virtual Hard Disk",
    "3.5",
    "Disk image file that serves as a virtual hard disk for Linux operating systems, such as Ubuntu, Kubuntu, Xubuntu, Edubuntu, and UbuntuStudio; can be mounted and viewed by the operating system as an actual hard disk; can be used to run multiple variations of Linux without needing to repartition the hard drive. Virtual hard disk files may use the compound file extension .virtual.disk.. Linux Recognized by the Linux operating system.",
